{
  "library": "bpmn",
  "description": "BPMN 2.0 process shapes, drawn from scratch to the standard notation and typed the way the generic icons are: an event, activity or gateway is a native outline plus an inner glyph. Each shape is placed as the presentation shape custom:bpmn/<name> (a branch the document schema already admits, so no schema change) and names its own flowchart kind, bpmn-<name>, whose default shape is that shape, so the DSL prints by kind and get_schema teaches an agent when to use it. Events are circles whose border weight tells them apart (single = start, double = intermediate, thick = end) and whose glyph gives the trigger (message, timer, error, signal, link); a filled glyph means the event or task throws or sends rather than catches. Activities are rounded rectangles with a task-type marker in the corner (a sub-process shows its plus marker at the bottom; a call activity has a thick border). Gateways are diamonds typed by a centred glyph (exclusive X, parallel +, inclusive O, event-based pentagon in a double ring, complex asterisk). Data objects, data stores and text annotations complete the artefact set. Pools and lanes are not here: use custom:swimlane/pool and custom:swimlane/lane, and parent a BPMN node to the lane it belongs to. Sequence flow is the existing `flow` edge kind; message-flow, bpmn-association and data-association are the BPMN edge kinds (see flowchart.json). `family` is event, activity, gateway, data or annotation; `position`, `border`, `glyph`, `placement` and `throwing` are drawing data both renderers read (web/src/model/bpmnShapes.ts, web/src/canvas/shapes.tsx and src/Draughtsman.Mcp/Rendering/SvgRenderer.cs), so the two cannot drift; `size` is the size the palette places the shape at (events and gateways are drawn to fill their box, so keep them square). `glyphs` are line art on a 24x24 grid in the icon library's element format; an element flagged `solid` is always filled with the stroke colour, and one flagged `detail` is drawn in the node's fill colour when the glyph is filled. Left out on purpose: see docs/bpmn.md.",
